he &%BinaryFunction &%MeasureFn, which takes a &%Number and a &%UnitOfMeasure as arguments. For example, 3 &%Meters is expressed as (&%MeasureFn 3 &%Meter). Instances of &%ConstantQuantity form a partial order (see &%PartialOrderingRelation) with the &%lessThan relation, since &%lessThan is a &%RelationExtendedToQuantities and &%lessThan is defined over the &%RealNumbers. The &%lessThan relation is not a total order (see &%TotalOrderingRelation) over the class &%ConstantQuantity since elements of some subclasses of &%ConstantQuantity (such as length quantities) are incomparable to elements of other subclasses of &%ConstantQuantity (such as mass quantities).'))],[-(s__subclass(s__TimeMeasure,s__ConstantQuantity))],[-(s__instance(s__TimeMeasure__t,s__SetOrClass))],[-(s__documentation(s__TimeMeasure,s__EnglishLanguage,'The class of temporal durations (instances of &%TimeDuration) and positions of &%TimePoints and &%TimeIntervals along the universal timeline (instances of &%TimePosition).'))],[-(s__subclass(s__TimeDuration,s__TimeMeasure))],[-(s__instance(s__TimeDuration__t,s__SetOrClass))],[-(s__documentation(s__TimeDuration,s__EnglishLanguage,'Any measure of length of time, with or without respect to the universal timeline.'))],[-(s__subclass(s__TimePosition,s__TimeMeasure))],[-(s__partition_3(s__TimePosition,s__TimeInterval,s__TimePoint))],[-(s__documentation(s__TimePosition,s__EnglishLanguage,'Any &%TimePoint or &%TimeInterval along the universal timeline from &%NegativeInfinity to &%PositiveInfinity.'))],[-(s__subclass(s__TimeInterval,s__TimePosition))],[-(s__instance(s__TimeInterval__t,s__SetOrClass))],[-(s__instance(s__TimePosition__t,s__SetOrClass))],[-(s__documentation(s__TimeInterval,s__EnglishLanguage,'An interval of time. Note that a &%TimeInterval has both an extent and a location on the universal timeline. Note too that a &%TimeInterval has no gaps, i.e. this class contains only convex time intervals.'))],[-(s__subclass(s__TimePoint,s__TimePosition))],[-(s__documentation(s__TimePoint,s__EnglishLanguage,'An extensionless point on the universal timeline. The &%TimePoints at which &%Processes occur can be known with various degrees of precision and approximation, but conceptually &%TimePoints are point-like and not interval-like. That is, it doesnt make sense to talk about how long a &%TimePoint lasts.'))],[-(s__subclass(s__FunctionQuantity,s__PhysicalQuantity))],[-(s__documentation(s__FunctionQuantity,s__EnglishLanguage,'A &%FunctionQuantity is a &%PhysicalQuantity that is returned by a &%Function that maps from one or more instances of &%ConstantQuantity to another instance of &%ConstantQuantity. For example, the velocity of a particle would be represented by a &%FunctionQuantity relating values of time (which are instances of &%ConstantQuantity) to values of distance (also instances of &%ConstantQuantity). Note that all elements of the range of the &%Function corresponding to a &%FunctionQuantity have the same physical dimension as the &%FunctionQuantity itself.'))],[-(s__subclass(s__UnaryConstantFunctionQuantity,s__FunctionQuantity))],[-(s__documentation(s__UnaryConstantFunctionQuantity,s__EnglishLanguage,'A &%subclass of &%FunctionQuantity, instances of which are returned by &%UnaryFunctions that map from one instance of the &%Class &%ConstantQuantity to another instance of the &%Class &%ConstantQuantity.'))],[-(s__subclass(s__TimeDependentQuantity,s__UnaryConstantFunctionQuantity))],[-(s__instance(s__TimeDependentQuantity__t,s__SetOrClass))],[-(s__instance(s__UnaryConstantFunctionQuantity__t,s__SetOrClass))],[-(s__documentation(s__TimeDependentQuantity,s__EnglishLanguage,'A &%UnaryConstantFunctionQuantity of continuous time. All instances of this &%Class are returned by &%Functions that map a time quantity into another &%ConstantQuantity such as temperature. For example, the temperature at the top of the Empire State Building is a &%TimeDependentQuantity, since its value depends on the time.'))],[-(s__subclass(s__